WEBVTT

00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:17.290
I just bought some of our oil stuff.

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.390
I'm going to be rich.

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.180
Mr. Powell said so.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.020
Why don't you buy some?

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.410
Oh, you wouldn't take a chance.

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:27.970
Well, what do you think you took when you married that traveling salesman?

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:35.520
Could I help you?

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:37.040
- I'd like to see Mr. Powell.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:39.240
- He's giving a sales talk in the lecture room.

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:40.810
Won't you be seated?

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:44.110
- Why, I wonder if I might listen to the lecture.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:45.710
- Certainly, if you wish.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:46.910
Go right down that corridor.

00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:49.530
It's the second door on your right.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:57.720
- Thank you.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.000
- This is a view of the amalgamated oil companies

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:06.870
field it joins ours it is one of the largest producing fields in south america what an

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:15.540
inspiring sight did you ever see anything more beautiful i haven't in a few short months our

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:20.440
field will bristle with producing wells just like the picture before you when you see a golden

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:27.760
opportunity like this friends are you going to pass it by i'm not i've invested every cent i own in

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:28.770
this project

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:49.170
that ladies and gentlemen concludes our picture but before you go there's just one thing more

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:54.590
I'd like to say to you now this is not a fly-by-night sales promotion scheme but an opportunity

00:02:54.590 --> 00:03:00.000
for you to invest in a legitimate enterprise that will return you a life income I don't

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.400
there is one of us here who could finance the drilling of a well alone but by putting our money

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:10.990
together our individual small sums become a collective giant who will open up the gates

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.350
of opportunity and happiness for everyone.

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:32.710
- When did you get back to civilization?

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.150
- You didn't expect me to stay in the jungle

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:35.270
the rest of my life, did you?

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.350
- Well, I was beginning to think you were going to.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.200
How are all the cannibals?

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:40.660
I see you stayed one jump ahead of them,

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.620
or are you too tough to make a good stew?

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:44.120
Sit down.

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:47.230
- No, no, I put them all on a vegetable diet.

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:48.250
- Well, that wouldn't surprise me.

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:50.640
You always did have a good line.

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.500
- I just listened to your sales talk.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:53.310
- You did?

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:57.470
What did you think of it?

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.360
- Well, not much.

00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:01.850
- Why?

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:04.340
- You didn't believe those promises, did you?

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:06.520
- Well, I'll admit I did exaggerate a little,

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.760
but it's a sweet proposition.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:12.210
- Perhaps, for the company.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.530
Did you take a good look at those people

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:15.660
you were talking to?

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:18.860
They've worked hard for the little they have,

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:19.860
and getting them to put their money

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.550
into a thing like this is wrong.

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:22.710
It's outright stealing.

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:24.900
- Wait a minute, wait a minute.

00:04:24.900 --> 00:04:27.400
- You can't escape the laws of retribution, Frank.

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.930
They're not man-made.

00:04:28.930 --> 00:04:30.000
- I'll admit what you say

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:35.090
true about some companies but this one is really on the level if i didn't think so would i have

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:40.830
put eleven thousand dollars of my own money in it you did that why of course and when the first

00:04:40.830 --> 00:04:47.890
well comes in i'm getting married oh she's a wonderful girl curtis i'll introduce you to her

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:58.560
and if the well doesn't come in don't worry it will marjorie this is my brother curtis

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.000
miss norton mr powell

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:00.640
How do you do?

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:01.500
How do you do, Miss Norton?

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:04.730
Curtis got tired of converting heathens, so he came up to work on me.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:06.490
Do you think there's any hope for him?

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:08.520
Well, there might be, if that well comes in.

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:10.290
Let's not worry about me.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:12.110
The point is, we have to worry about you.

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:15.250
While he's here, it's up to me to see that he's properly entertained.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:20.150
You know, hot shows, cabarets, maybe a gambling club or two, and all the best cocktail bars.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:21.650
That's what I like about Frank.

00:05:21.690 --> 00:05:22.970
His taste is so appropriate.

00:05:22.970 --> 00:05:26.350
Hey, speaking of taste, how about having dinner at your apartment tonight?

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:28.430
You know, just to sort of celebrate the occasion?

00:05:29.090 --> 00:05:30.000
Well, I'm afraid that will call you

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:34.990
Oh no, no, why not at all. Marjorie loves to cook. Besides, it'll give me a chance to

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:42.080
show you exactly why I picked her out of 50,000 applicants. See, it's getting near quitting

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:46.640
time. Suppose you and Marjorie run along and I'll join you later. I've got a lot of work

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:52.360
to do here, but it won't take me over an hour. And, uh, could we have some of that famous

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:54.860
Swiss steak with the nickel-sized biscuits?

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:56.810
Yes, sir.

00:05:56.810 --> 00:06:00.000
Oh, and if you hurry, you'll just have time to make a lemonade.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.110
Yes, sir.

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:02.110
I'll get my coat.

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:11.420
I'll wait here.

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:12.500
Come in.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:16.080
Hello, Mrs. Harding.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.490
Frank, may I speak to you a moment, please?

00:06:20.490 --> 00:06:23.170
Certainly.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:24.470
Come in.

00:06:24.470 --> 00:06:25.470
Yes, sir.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:26.420
I'll get my coat.

00:06:26.420 --> 00:06:27.140
I'll wait here.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:37.440
sit down make yourself comfortable thank you now what can i do for you you remember joe don't you

00:06:37.440 --> 00:06:42.990
well yes he's down in south america now and i've just had a letter from him that's made me terribly

00:06:42.990 --> 00:06:56.060
anxious about my oil staff if the company says they are about to bring in a well they're lying

00:06:56.060 --> 00:07:00.000
to you you'd better look into it i can't understand it

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:08.130
After that, here's our latest report. We're drilling three wells at once down there, and

00:07:08.130 --> 00:07:10.550
our number one well is down 4,200 feet.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:12.950
I guess Jill must be mistaken.

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:18.380
I'm sure that he is. May I keep this letter, Miss Harding? Thank you. Now, don't you worry

00:07:18.380 --> 00:07:19.650
about a thing.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:24.890
I knew I was right in coming to you. Sarah wanted me to go straight to the police, but

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:30.000
I said, "No, sir. I'm going to talk it over with Frank. I knew you were right."

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.210
wouldn't be selling stock if there was anything crooked. Thank you Miss Hardy. I

00:07:34.210 --> 00:07:39.050
appreciate your confidence in me. You go on home, don't you worry about a thing.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:43.150
It's a perfectly legitimate deal and everything is going to turn out all right.

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:46.070
Good night. Good night.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:10.610
What sort of progress are we making at the field, Carlton?

00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:12.550
Why, haven't you seen the reports?

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:13.880
I've seen them all right.

00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.750
But what I want to know is, are they correct?

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:16.530
Why, of course not.

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:17.700
Certainly they're correct.

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:19.220
What do you mean by asking such a question?

00:08:19.220 --> 00:08:20.640
Just this.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:22.730
Here's a letter from a Mrs. Hardy.

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:24.170
A nephew of us is down there, and he

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.880
says there's absolutely no drilling going on at all.

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:28.930
How about it, Carlton?

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:30.000
Why, oh, that's ridiculous.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:31.960
Is that true?

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:35.540
Why ask him? I'm in charge of operations.

00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:37.460
I'll tell you the man doesn't know what he's talking about.

00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.370
Are you sure?

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:40.960
Don't be a fool, Powell.

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:42.510
Maybe I have been already.

00:08:42.510 --> 00:08:45.110
I've done a lot of talking about how honest this company is.

00:08:45.110 --> 00:08:47.560
I've taken money from people who can't afford to lose it.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:52.040
I've even sold all my friends on this proposition and I've invested a lot of my own money in it.

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:54.830
I think you're getting yourself all worked up over nothing, Powell.

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:57.170
Why, certainly.

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:59.570
My nephew's probably trying to stir up trouble.

00:09:01.150 --> 00:09:04.010
We'll give this hardy woman her money back if she's not satisfied.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:05.540
That won't satisfy me.

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:09.600
I've never seen the field and I'm not going to sell another share of stock until I do.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:11.710
You mean, you want to go down there?

00:09:11.710 --> 00:09:13.450
As fast as the plane will take me.

00:09:13.450 --> 00:09:16.110
Well, I suggest that you wait until after the sales campaign.

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:17.970
We can't spare you right now, Powell.

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:19.420
I'm not waiting for anything.

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:21.460
I've known you a long time, Carlton.

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:23.960
I've taken your word for everything that went on around here.

00:09:23.960 --> 00:09:26.740
But if there's anything crooked, you'll pay for it.

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:28.680
And that goes for you too, gentlemen.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.120
Get me South American Airways.

00:09:42.880 --> 00:09:49.250
South American Airway, when is your next plane leave for Miami?

00:09:50.110 --> 00:09:50.750
Tomorrow morning.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.750
Is there another leaving here that connects with it?

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:56.180
Forty minutes?

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:58.540
Make a reservation right away.

00:09:58.640 --> 00:09:59.120
Frank Powell.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.140
- C-O-W-E-double-L.

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:08.900
That's right, get me circle three four seven hundred.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:11.230
Hello, is Miss Norton in?

00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:12.740
This is Mr. Powell speaking.

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:14.010
I want to leave a message for her.

00:10:14.010 --> 00:10:15.910
Tell her something has happened that makes it necessary

00:10:15.910 --> 00:10:17.790
for me to leave town immediately.

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:19.980
I'll explain to her when I get back.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:28.600
Thank you, yes, goodbye.

00:10:28.600 --> 00:10:30.000
- Why didn't you try to buy more?

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:31.760
We wouldn't have had a chance with him.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:34.870
I told you we shouldn't have used that money.

00:10:34.870 --> 00:10:35.920
So what?

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:39.920
We took a chance on the market and lost.

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:43.830
We'd won, we'd have been patting each other on the back.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:47.160
What are we going to do?

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:50.440
We can't stand an investigation at this time.

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:53.620
We might move to a healthier climate.

00:10:53.620 --> 00:10:54.710
Yes.

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:57.340
Hal can't get back in less than a week.

00:10:57.340 --> 00:10:59.180
That ought to give us a good start.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:02.470
Yes. That's all right for you two.

00:11:03.630 --> 00:11:04.830
But I have a wife and family.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:07.560
It means ruin and disgrace to them.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:10.750
It's a little too late to think about that now.

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:14.830
Come on, Burns. Let's go over the accounts.

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.240
Might as well get it all while we're waiting.

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:18.040
Right.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:25.280
my dear family, I was persuaded by my two partners to join them in using some of the

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:29.220
company's funds for personal speculation.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:37.270
cannot bear the thought of facing those with whom I have broken faith, nor the disgrace

00:12:37.270 --> 00:12:48.430
I have brought on you, whom I love. That is why I am taking my own life. With my last

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:55.590
breath, I ask your forgiveness. William Carlton.

00:13:18.620 --> 00:13:25.480
much does that make? 26,000. That's 13,000 apiece. What about cotton?

00:13:34.380 --> 00:13:40.930
by the fool now we'll have to clear out of here in a hurry maybe we won't have

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:47.910
to clear out of here at all now what do you mean he carried a hundred thousand

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:53.750
dollar life insurance made out to the firm pay off on suicide he's not old

00:13:53.750 --> 00:14:00.000
enough maybe not but it pays double for violent death look up 20 morocco

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:14.660
phone number. This isn't suicide. It's murder. Your boy sure folded up like a punctured balloon

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:19.750
when O'Brien socked him last night. That's all right, Tony. He wasn't in condition. None of your

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:26.430
fighters ever are. They couldn't even box oranges. They're doing all right, and so am I. Yeah, am I.

00:14:26.810 --> 00:14:28.830
When I make bets with ham and eggers like you,

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.610
Quit stinking that desk.

00:14:31.990 --> 00:14:33.670
I just paid ten bucks to have it refinished.

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:34.390
Okay.

00:14:35.900 --> 00:14:36.860
There's your two grand.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:38.960
You're sure it's all here?

00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:41.500
You wouldn't know unless somebody counted it for you.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:47.350
Yeah?

00:14:47.670 --> 00:14:49.270
It's Tony Marock.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:50.800
This is George Richards.

00:14:51.890 --> 00:14:54.350
I've got a little job for a couple of your boys.

00:14:56.180 --> 00:14:57.580
No, he's that way already.

00:14:58.900 --> 00:14:59.930
Now meet me across the street.

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:05.580
in about 20 minutes.

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:08.750
Speculating was done in Carlton's name.

00:15:08.750 --> 00:15:12.220
Get circle 78200.

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:13.820
We claimed that we didn't know anything about it

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:14.980
and make good from the insurance money,

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:16.300
the amounts that he took.

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:20.290
That ought to satisfy everybody.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:22.570
This is Mr. Carlton, Briggs.

00:15:22.570 --> 00:15:24.870
Tell Mrs. Carlton that I had to go to Mr. Powell's

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.550
apartment on business.

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:27.780
I won't be home to dinner.

00:16:05.470 --> 00:16:07.210
- Your name's Frank Powell?

00:16:07.210 --> 00:16:07.940
- Yes.

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:09.190
- Well, you run for arrest.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:10.520
- Arrest?

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:11.360
For what?

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:14.090
- For the murder of William Carlton.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:16.100
- Carlton?

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:16.920
Murdered?

00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:17.670
- Yes, murdered.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:37.820
Carlton came to your apartment to confess and throw himself upon your mercy.

00:16:38.330 --> 00:16:42.820
You got in an argument with him, killed him, and tried to escape to South America.

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:46.510
I didn't kill Carlton. I swear I didn't. I swear it.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:54.150
Nine to three for conviction. Let's review this evidence again.

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:58.960
I heard him threaten Carlton. He said Carlton, if there's any crookedness in this, you pay for it.

00:16:59.190 --> 00:17:00.000
Those were his excuses.

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:04.820
Mr. Paul phoned and asked me to tell Miss Norton that he had to leave town immediately.

00:17:04.820 --> 00:17:06.740
I was expecting him for dinner.

00:17:06.740 --> 00:17:08.850
I was in a hurry to catch a plane.

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:10.740
Mr. Carlton left the office to go to Mr. Paul's apartment.

00:17:10.740 --> 00:17:13.740
I never saw Carlton after I left the office.

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:14.690
I answered the phone.

00:17:14.690 --> 00:17:16.690
Mr. Carlton said he wouldn't be home for dinner.

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:18.690
He had to go to Mr. Paul's apartment on business.

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:22.870
I saw Mr. Paul come out of his apartment with a suitcase and run down the hall.

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:23.920
He looked excited.

00:17:23.920 --> 00:17:27.930
And when I unlocked Mr. Paul's apartment to go in and clean it up,

00:17:27.930 --> 00:17:30.000
I saw his body like this.

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:35.520
furniture was upset and broken there's been a fight the body was lying face down

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:39.900
but I didn't find a gun death was due to a bullet in the right temple fired at

00:17:39.900 --> 00:17:44.050
close range examination of the body revealed numerous bruises which could

00:17:44.050 --> 00:17:57.880
have been incurred in a struggle I were guilty but I didn't kill Carlton I didn't

00:17:57.880 --> 00:18:00.000
I know that Frank it was Richardson

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:04.470
and Burns. They killed him for the insurance money. Can't anybody but me see that? It isn't

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:09.660
what we think. We must prove it. The insurance company investigators and private detectives

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:13.290
are working on that angle now. If I could get out of here for an hour, I'd prove it.

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:19.020
I'd make them confess and I'd blow their heads off. Take it easy, boy. Thoughts like

00:18:19.020 --> 00:18:25.100
that won't do you any good. You must have faith. Faith that Wright will prevail. Faith

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:30.000
in your... Faith? How much faith would you have if you were in my place? If they were taking you

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:35.090
prison if you had to sit in a cell day after day thinking of all the things you had to live for

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:41.240
and all the reasons why you didn't want to die how much faith would i only wish i could go in

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:53.430
your place frank i'm sorry i guess it's my nerves nothing happens without a reason though sometimes

00:18:53.430 --> 00:19:00.000
it is hard to understand remember what i said that day in your office about making money the wrong way

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:01.290
And retribution?

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:04.850
Come now, put yourself together.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:06.530
Marjorie's waiting to see you.

00:19:30.190 --> 00:19:30.630
Frank.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:31.890
Hello, honey.

00:19:32.760 --> 00:19:33.500
Gee, you look pretty.

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:34.630
New outfit?

00:19:35.050 --> 00:19:35.880
Of course not.

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:37.190
Don't you remember it?

00:19:38.060 --> 00:19:38.700
Oh, sure.

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:39.360
Sure.

00:19:39.660 --> 00:19:42.000
Why, that's the outfit you wore the day we went to the fair.

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:44.130
The day I asked you to be...

00:19:44.130 --> 00:19:44.450
No.

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:45.320
No.

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:47.660
This is the one I wore to the amusement park.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:52.240
The day our boat got stuck in the old mill tunnel and...

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:54.830
How's the cooking coming along?

00:19:55.380 --> 00:19:55.880
Fine.

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:57.850
I've got a new pie recipe.

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:00.000
You make the crust with vanilla wafers.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:02.650
Come on, pal. It's time to go with the train.

00:20:03.210 --> 00:20:04.420
Can you put whipped cream on it?

00:20:04.670 --> 00:20:05.960
It's nearly all whipped cream.

00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:07.720
I know. I'll like it, then.

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:09.550
Will you make one real soon?

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:11.450
I'll make one for your birthday.

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:13.660
And we'll put candles in the middle of it.

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:14.570
And light them.

00:20:15.240 --> 00:20:17.100
And it'll probably look so funny.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:19.720
We'll both sit there and laugh.

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:30.000
Come on!

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.320
Come on, step on it. The train's ready to pull out.

00:20:32.400 --> 00:20:35.760
I'll let it go. This is one train I wouldn't mind missing.

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:40.660
Yeah, excuse me, pal.

00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:44.850
Hey, give it back to him.

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:09.520
- What did I do with that handcuffed key?

00:21:09.520 --> 00:21:14.520
Did I give it to you?

00:21:14.520 --> 00:21:17.410
- Let's have it.

00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:20.120
Come on.

00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:21.140
- I was just kidding.

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:24.140
- Yeah, you can't even be honest on your way to the pen.

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:27.270
Get around.

00:21:27.270 --> 00:21:28.100
- All aboard.

00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:43.250
- He's going up for a minute. - Yes, but I'm innocent.

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:46.160
So am I. They're railroading me too.

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:48.370
I never stole nothing in my life.

00:21:49.050 --> 00:21:52.150
- How about getting a little air in here? - Get away from that window.

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:55.570
- This car here is air-conditioned. - Yeah?

00:21:55.820 --> 00:21:58.840
You coppers in here, the air conditioner ain't good enough.

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:03.360
You mug! Don't you try any of that stuff with me!

00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:05.890
I ought to smack you one right in the jaw.

00:22:05.890 --> 00:22:07.810
Oh, what are you getting peeved about?

00:22:07.810 --> 00:22:10.560
You don't have to pay for it. Tell him to put it on my bill.

00:22:44.620 --> 00:22:46.340
- Hiya, boss. - Here we are.

00:22:46.860 --> 00:22:49.270
- Who's this guy? - He was going up for a murder rap.

00:22:49.490 --> 00:22:52.770
- We couldn't take Gabby without him? - Yeah, how about getting off these bracelets?

00:22:52.870 --> 00:22:55.670
- I'm tired of doing this sister act. - Okay, Case.

00:22:56.270 --> 00:22:59.830
Sure sprung me neat, boss. I gotta hand it to you. You're a right guy to work for.

00:23:00.220 --> 00:23:02.020
You ain't working for me no more, Gabby.

00:23:02.410 --> 00:23:04.130
You're all washed up.

00:23:05.500 --> 00:23:05.780
Oh.

00:23:07.080 --> 00:23:07.680
You heard me.

00:23:08.250 --> 00:23:10.750
I told you I'd spring you loose, and I did.

00:23:11.920 --> 00:23:13.980
Nobody's going to work for me and work for himself, too.

00:23:14.590 --> 00:23:15.910
You like to pull jobs alone?

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:17.030
So hop to it.

00:23:17.630 --> 00:23:18.990
Oh, boss, you're kidding.

00:23:19.310 --> 00:23:19.710
Am I?

00:23:22.010 --> 00:23:23.010
Here's a rod for you.

00:23:23.500 --> 00:23:24.480
Here's 20 bucks.

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:28.800
Now get out of this town and forget that you've ever been here, if you know what's good for you.

00:23:30.030 --> 00:23:34.910
- Here, buddy, same thing goes for you.

00:23:34.910 --> 00:23:37.970
- Thanks, I'll see that you get this back.

00:23:37.970 --> 00:23:38.890
- Forget it.

00:23:38.890 --> 00:23:41.330
- Well, so long, boss.

00:23:41.330 --> 00:23:43.030
So long, fella, so long, Gabby.

00:23:43.030 --> 00:23:43.860
- Whose draw is it?

00:23:43.860 --> 00:23:56.100
- Your draw.

00:23:56.100 --> 00:23:59.340
- Pal, here's just what we need to scram out of town.

00:23:59.340 --> 00:24:00.000
What do you say we want?

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:08.380
borrow it. You go ahead. I'm not leaving. You ain't. Good luck. Wait a minute. I'll give you $20

00:24:08.380 --> 00:24:27.570
for that gun. Okay. Why, I... That's all right, pal. I already collected. Here's your gun. So long. So long.

00:24:31.690 --> 00:24:36.120
- What can we do now? - We mustn't give up hope.

00:24:36.120 --> 00:24:39.830
- You mean you still believe he has a chance? - Yes, more than ever.

00:24:39.830 --> 00:24:49.030
Here, here's my engagement ring. We can raise some money on it.

00:24:49.030 --> 00:25:00.000
- We're from headquarters. We want to look around.

00:25:01.600 --> 00:25:02.160
Go ahead, Mac.

00:25:02.650 --> 00:25:03.710
What's the meaning of this?

00:25:04.150 --> 00:25:04.940
Don't you know?

00:25:05.400 --> 00:25:06.810
If I did, I wouldn't have asked you.

00:25:07.410 --> 00:25:08.860
You've been here since 6 o'clock?

00:25:09.530 --> 00:25:09.930
Yes.

00:25:10.270 --> 00:25:11.750
And nothing unexpected happened?

00:25:12.160 --> 00:25:13.540
Why, what do you mean?

00:25:15.240 --> 00:25:17.290
Frank Powell escaped.

00:25:31.820 --> 00:25:32.900
Where's Richards?

00:25:32.900 --> 00:25:35.120
Why, uh, who is it, Burns?

00:25:35.120 --> 00:25:36.440
Come over here.

00:25:36.440 --> 00:25:41.130
All right, out with it.

00:25:41.130 --> 00:25:45.170
You two killed Carlton for the insurance money, didn't you?

00:25:45.170 --> 00:25:48.020
Tell me the truth, Harrell!

00:25:48.020 --> 00:25:52.130
Well, I guess you've got us, Powell.

00:25:52.130 --> 00:25:54.920
We killed him.

00:25:54.920 --> 00:25:56.120
And framed me.

00:25:56.120 --> 00:25:58.680
I ought to put a bullet in the both of you.

00:25:58.680 --> 00:26:00.000
But that would be too quick.

00:26:04.540 --> 00:26:09.510
Get me to the police station.

00:26:09.510 --> 00:26:11.790
I want you two to go through what I did.

00:26:11.790 --> 00:26:15.470
Looking forward to that electric chair.

00:26:15.470 --> 00:26:16.560
Hello, police?

00:26:16.560 --> 00:26:19.430
Send up a couple of men to 926 West 10th Street.

00:26:19.430 --> 00:26:20.880
Apartment 211.

00:26:20.880 --> 00:26:22.050
That's right.

00:26:22.050 --> 00:26:24.000
This is Frank Powell speaking.

00:26:24.000 --> 00:26:29.400
Powell?

00:26:29.400 --> 00:26:30.000
Been waiting a long time.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:30.900
Frank!

00:26:30.900 --> 00:26:33.110
Curtis!

00:26:33.110 --> 00:26:35.090
I thought I'd find you here.

00:26:35.090 --> 00:26:36.090
They've confessed.

00:26:36.090 --> 00:26:37.080
I told you I'd make them.

00:26:37.080 --> 00:26:39.050
The police are on their way here now.

00:26:39.050 --> 00:26:40.050
They won't take them, Frank.

00:26:40.050 --> 00:26:41.050
They'll take you.

00:26:41.050 --> 00:26:42.050
Did you hear what I said?

00:26:42.050 --> 00:26:43.050
They've confessed.

00:26:43.050 --> 00:26:45.160
Confession at the point of a gun means nothing.

00:26:45.160 --> 00:26:46.620
You knew that.

00:26:46.620 --> 00:26:50.210
Well, this time you'll have something to send me to the J4.

00:26:50.210 --> 00:26:51.160
Don't, Frank.

00:26:51.160 --> 00:26:52.160
Keep out of this, Curtis.

00:26:52.160 --> 00:26:53.160
Give me that gun.

00:26:53.160 --> 00:26:54.160
You don't know what you're doing.

00:26:54.160 --> 00:26:55.160
Keep out of this!

00:26:55.160 --> 00:26:56.980
I'm trying to take charge of this gun.

00:26:56.980 --> 00:26:57.880
The police can't hear.

00:26:57.880 --> 00:27:00.000
You can't turn him in.

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:05.490
him over to the police? Can't I? But you're sending an innocent man to the chair. The law says he's

00:27:05.490 --> 00:27:11.280
guilty. Isn't it possible for the law to be mistaken? That isn't for me to worry about. What the law says

00:27:11.280 --> 00:27:30.000
goes. Is that final? Yeah. Save your breath. Come on. I thought I was working things out. I've only made them worse.

00:27:31.150 --> 00:27:32.760
Well, you shouldn't have done it, Curtis.

00:27:32.760 --> 00:27:36.370
Did you think I was going to stand by and let them take you back?

00:27:36.370 --> 00:27:38.870
But now they'll take you to prison for helping me.

00:27:38.870 --> 00:27:41.810
You were set free for a reason, Frank.

00:27:41.810 --> 00:27:43.680
Perhaps to gain time.

00:27:43.680 --> 00:27:48.280
If that's the way it's to be worked out, I'm not afraid.

00:27:48.280 --> 00:27:52.500
What you should do now is go away and hide until the truth comes out.

00:27:52.500 --> 00:27:53.970
Which it will.

00:27:53.970 --> 00:27:55.960
Have you any money?

00:27:55.960 --> 00:27:56.760
No.

00:28:01.660 --> 00:28:03.560
Why, that's Marjorie's engagement ring.

00:28:03.560 --> 00:28:05.700
She gave it to me to raise money to help you.

00:28:05.700 --> 00:28:09.580
Do you know where we can get a loan on it tonight?

00:28:09.580 --> 00:28:12.440
I think I do.

00:28:12.440 --> 00:28:16.710
Drive to 3rd and Tucker on the east side.

00:28:30.960 --> 00:28:31.940
What are you doing here?

00:28:32.210 --> 00:28:34.700
I came back to see if you could let me have some money on this.

00:28:35.860 --> 00:28:36.540
Who's the deacon?

00:28:37.020 --> 00:28:38.460
He's my brother, a missionary.

00:28:39.000 --> 00:28:40.390
You're in bad company, Mish.

00:28:41.310 --> 00:28:42.550
Come to my office.

00:28:43.000 --> 00:28:44.500
Ryan's just coming up the front stairs now.

00:28:44.710 --> 00:28:45.010
Ryan?

00:28:45.170 --> 00:28:45.430
Yes.

00:28:45.930 --> 00:28:46.580
He's a cop.

00:28:47.040 --> 00:28:47.630
Come with me.

00:28:48.990 --> 00:28:51.510
Get into that second door of the locker room.

00:29:10.520 --> 00:29:11.840
- Hello, Ryan.

00:29:11.840 --> 00:29:13.910
- Hello, Sparks.

00:29:13.910 --> 00:29:15.360
Meet Bill Scully.

00:29:15.360 --> 00:29:16.730
He's new in the district.

00:29:16.730 --> 00:29:18.090
- How are you?

00:29:18.090 --> 00:29:20.050
Up after curfew, ain't you?

00:29:20.050 --> 00:29:21.650
- Yeah.

00:29:21.650 --> 00:29:24.750
Gabby Holt got lifted off the train last night,

00:29:24.750 --> 00:29:26.570
and the chief is kind of put out

00:29:26.570 --> 00:29:28.930
because he got away with a pair of new bracelets.

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:32.180
wouldn't know where I would find him, do you?

00:29:32.180 --> 00:29:34.110
No, I wouldn't.

00:29:34.110 --> 00:29:38.000
I figured you wouldn't.

00:29:38.000 --> 00:29:40.440
Jabby Holt didn't have him on him when we picked him up

00:29:40.440 --> 00:29:43.570
a little while ago in a wrecked car he had stolen.

00:29:43.570 --> 00:29:46.130
So they must be on the other fellow that was pinned to him

00:29:46.130 --> 00:29:50.420
on the train, a guy named Powell.

00:29:50.420 --> 00:29:53.210
He was on his way to the chair.

00:29:53.210 --> 00:29:56.390
You mean the guys that were handcuffed together got away?

00:29:56.390 --> 00:29:57.220
Yeah.

00:29:57.220 --> 00:30:00.000
What was the matter with the guys?

00:30:00.000 --> 00:30:18.310
cards. Did they fall asleep? Yeah. They were up late the night before playing cards. Say do you mind if I show Bill around? He's never been in an athletic club before. Sure. Help yourself.

00:30:36.170 --> 00:30:36.630
Excuse me.

00:31:08.970 --> 00:31:13.090
- Did you find anything? - Yeah, a hairpin.

00:31:19.270 --> 00:31:25.000
You're new around here, aren't you? Where are you from?

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:34.510
get Mish away from Ryan put him in the ring with roundhouse but he ain't no

00:31:34.510 --> 00:31:38.150
fighter what's the difference if he gets knocked cold he can't answer Ryan's

00:31:38.150 --> 00:31:47.160
questions hey Mish get in the ring take it easy roundhouse you've had a pretty

00:31:47.160 --> 00:31:54.000
good workout already hey you sure ain't something done look you can always tell

00:31:54.000 --> 00:32:00.000
those pork and beaters they'll fall for that gag anytime all right

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:02.000
Give me all you got, but look out for your buttons.

00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:06.280
Come on, let's see.

00:32:06.280 --> 00:32:09.310
What a guy, huh?

00:32:09.310 --> 00:32:10.330
Look out for my right hand.

00:32:10.330 --> 00:32:17.140
Oh, is that slow?

00:32:17.140 --> 00:32:26.130
I've seen that guy somewhere before.

00:32:26.130 --> 00:32:27.080
Yeah?

00:32:27.080 --> 00:32:30.000
Maybe you've seen him fightin' down here.

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:57.010
New York. Maybe so, but I've never been in New York. Pretty good, huh? He's too good for you, Roundhouse. Hey, the shoelace is undone. No, it isn't, but yours is. Where'd you learn to fight like that? College. Hey, you'd better send Roundhouse to college.

00:33:02.460 --> 00:33:15.360
Hello Tony, this is Sparks, yeah? Same to you and many of 'em. Listen, Roundhouse can't fight on the 15th. He broke his jaw.

00:33:15.360 --> 00:33:17.040
What'd he do, fall out of bed?

00:33:17.040 --> 00:33:20.580
No, he tripped over his shoelace.

00:33:20.580 --> 00:33:22.260
Hey, what are you doing here?

00:33:22.260 --> 00:33:26.180
Listen, I'm telling you this because I'm calling off that four grand bet.

00:33:26.180 --> 00:33:29.440
What do you mean you're calling it off? You can't crawfish in no bet with me.

00:33:30.030 --> 00:33:31.830
Roundhouse can't fight but one of your other boys in.

00:33:32.430 --> 00:33:33.760
That bet still goes.

00:33:38.410 --> 00:33:39.110
He won't do it.

00:33:41.180 --> 00:33:43.540
You've got to take Roundhouse's place on the 15th, Mish.

00:33:44.300 --> 00:33:47.300
That's absurd.

00:33:47.820 --> 00:33:49.800
But you said you were the inter-college champ.

00:33:50.400 --> 00:33:52.600
Yes, but that was a long time ago.

00:33:52.950 --> 00:33:54.550
Yeah, but you didn't do the bad out there.

00:33:55.080 --> 00:33:56.460
And Tony's boy ain't no champ.

00:33:56.700 --> 00:33:58.790
You're crazy, Sparks. He hasn't got a champ.

00:33:58.830 --> 00:34:00.000
Well, who have we got to go with?

00:34:00.480 --> 00:34:02.660
Now listen, you got me into this and you're going to get me out.

00:34:02.910 --> 00:34:03.790
I'm holding him.

00:34:04.630 --> 00:34:07.450
And if you don't win the fight on the 15th, I turn him back to the police.

00:34:09.450 --> 00:34:12.040
And if I do win it?

00:34:12.430 --> 00:34:13.910
I'll give you 500 bucks.

00:34:14.710 --> 00:34:17.260
And give you back your own ring.

00:34:32.040 --> 00:34:32.890
- What's the matter?

00:34:32.890 --> 00:34:34.200
I got a cholly horse.

00:34:34.200 --> 00:34:35.480
- Maybe we'd better turn back.

00:34:35.480 --> 00:34:38.190
- No, no, you go ahead, I'll wait for you here.

00:34:38.190 --> 00:34:39.310
- All right, take it easy.

00:34:39.310 --> 00:34:56.420
- All right, don't mention it, Miss Benson.

00:34:56.420 --> 00:34:59.380
Remember, he's in training.

00:35:06.490 --> 00:35:07.500
- Good morning.

00:35:07.500 --> 00:35:08.960
- Nice day, isn't it?

00:35:08.960 --> 00:35:10.620
- Yes, it is.

00:35:10.620 --> 00:35:12.100
- It's been yesterday morning.

00:35:12.100 --> 00:35:13.950
- Is it?

00:35:13.950 --> 00:35:16.270
- Nice as the day before.

00:35:16.270 --> 00:35:18.080
- Isn't it?

00:35:18.080 --> 00:35:19.600
- I had all the weather questions.

00:35:19.600 --> 00:35:22.080
Why didn't you come to my party last night?

00:35:22.080 --> 00:35:25.580
- Sorry, but that's against training regulations.

00:35:25.580 --> 00:35:28.490
- Don't you ever do anything you shouldn't?

00:35:28.490 --> 00:35:29.600
- I try not to.

00:35:30.700 --> 00:35:33.620
- I'm not used to having my invitations ignored.

00:35:33.620 --> 00:35:35.990
- I'm not an offense, Miss Vincent.

00:35:35.990 --> 00:35:39.470
- My friends call me Helen.

00:35:39.470 --> 00:35:41.970
- I'm afraid seeing you six mornings on the bridle path

00:35:41.970 --> 00:35:43.670
hardly gives me that privilege.

00:35:43.670 --> 00:35:46.520
- Oh, so that's it.

00:35:46.520 --> 00:35:48.560
Well, see you again sometime.

00:35:48.560 --> 00:35:59.200
Goodbye.

00:35:59.200 --> 00:35:59.800
Hey, fellas.

00:36:17.920 --> 00:36:21.510
- Something wrong, lady?

00:36:21.510 --> 00:36:24.280
- Will you beat it?

00:36:24.280 --> 00:36:25.990
- Are you having a fit?

00:36:25.990 --> 00:36:27.330
- No, I'm not having a fit.

00:36:27.330 --> 00:36:29.390
I'm unconscious, can't you see?

00:36:29.390 --> 00:36:30.000
Now beat it.

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:31.780
- Go away, beat it.

00:36:31.780 --> 00:36:34.730
- Are you sure you ain't crazy?

00:37:00.380 --> 00:37:01.960
Helen, can you hear me?

00:37:01.960 --> 00:37:03.300
Helen!

00:37:03.300 --> 00:37:05.220
Well, mister, there ain't no need to get head up.

00:37:05.220 --> 00:37:07.550
Help!

00:37:07.550 --> 00:37:10.140
Where can I get some water?

00:37:10.140 --> 00:37:13.610
Well, you might throw her in the creek right over there.

00:37:13.610 --> 00:37:22.980
And I thought Matilda was touched in the head.

00:37:36.840 --> 00:37:38.260
What are you doing back here?

00:37:38.260 --> 00:37:42.040
I came back to get warm. That mesh is colder than a cake of ice.

00:37:42.040 --> 00:37:43.960
You mean he wouldn't give you a tumble?

00:37:43.960 --> 00:37:45.720
That's just what I mean.

00:37:45.720 --> 00:37:47.140
The guy ain't human.

00:37:47.140 --> 00:37:50.140
I'd rather make love to the Sphinx.

00:37:50.140 --> 00:37:51.540
Who's he?

00:37:51.540 --> 00:37:53.520
He's an Egyptian.

00:37:53.520 --> 00:37:55.570
Oh, an Egyptian, huh?

00:37:55.570 --> 00:37:56.690
Where'd you meet him?

00:37:56.690 --> 00:37:58.930
He's a statue.

00:38:02.840 --> 00:38:04.800
You should have stayed up there and kept trying.

00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:10.280
Say, when a guy carries me four miles in his arms and don't even crack a smile, I'm through.

00:38:11.020 --> 00:38:12.200
I guess you're slipping.

00:38:13.490 --> 00:38:15.110
I gotta spoil this fight some way.

00:38:15.660 --> 00:38:16.840
That mish is dynamite.

00:38:17.260 --> 00:38:18.080
I watched him work.

00:38:18.440 --> 00:38:19.740
Why'd you call off the bet?

00:38:20.000 --> 00:38:21.220
Sparks wanted to.

00:38:21.880 --> 00:38:23.080
That's an idea.

00:38:24.760 --> 00:38:26.160
Smokey, I'm gonna buy you a new knife.

00:38:35.020 --> 00:38:38.480
- Sparks, I've been thinking things over.

00:38:38.480 --> 00:38:40.060
You and I oughta quit trying to get the best

